{"name":"Ice Castle","hex":"#d5edfb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ice castle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of ice palace."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ice_castle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ice palace","blocks":[{"text":"An ice palace or ice castle is a castle-like structure made of blocks of ice. These blocks are usually harvested from nearby rivers or lakes when they become frozen in winter. The first known ice palace appeared in St. Petersburg, Russia, when Anna Ivanovna, Empress of Russia, commissioned an ice palace in St. Petersburg, Russia, during the winter of 1739–40. Architect Piotr Eropkin and scientist Georg Wolfgang Krafft used huge ice blocks measuring 16 m (52 ft) long by 5 m (16 ft) wide, joined together with frozen water, to build the palace. The city recreates the ice palace every winter."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice_palace"},{"title":"Frost flower","blocks":[{"text":"A frost flower or ice flower is formed when thin layers of ice are extruded from long-stemmed plants in autumn or early winter. The thin layers of ice are often formed into exquisite patterns, curling into \"petals\" which resemble flowers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Frost_flower_Ozarks_01.jpg/330px-Frost_flower_Ozarks_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frost_flower"},{"title":"Ice","blocks":[{"text":"Ice is water that is frozen into a solid state, typically forming at or below temperatures of 0 °C, 32 °F, or 273.15 K. It occurs naturally on Earth, on other planets, in Oort cloud objects, and as interstellar ice. As a naturally occurring crystalline inorganic solid with an ordered structure, ice is considered to be a mineral. Depending on the presence of impurities such as particles of soil or bubbles of air, it can appear transparent or a more or less opaque bluish-white color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg/330px-Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice"},{"title":"Castle","blocks":[{"text":"A castle is a type of fortified structure built during the Middle Ages predominantly by the nobility or royalty and by military orders. Scholars usually consider a castle to be the private fortified residence of a lord or noble. This is distinct from a mansion, palace, and villa, whose main purpose was exclusively for pleasance and are not primarily fortresses but may be fortified. Use of the term has varied over time and, sometimes, has also been applied to structures such as hill forts and 19th- and 20th-century homes built to resemble castles. Over the Middle Ages, when genuine castles were built, they took on a great many forms with many different features, although some, such as curtain walls, arrowslits, and portcullises, were commonplace."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Panor%C3%A1mica_Oto%C3%B1o_Alc%C3%A1zar_de_Segovia.jpg/330px-Panor%C3%A1mica_Oto%C3%B1o_Alc%C3%A1zar_de_Segovia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castle"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Valery_Jacobi_Ice_House.jpg/500px-Valery_Jacobi_Ice_House.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Valery_Jacobi_Ice_House.jpg/1280px-Valery_Jacobi_Ice_House.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Valery_Jacobi_Ice_House.jpg/500px-Valery_Jacobi_Ice_House.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"In this 1878 painting by Valery Jacobi, the scared newly-weds sit on the icy bed to the left; the jocular woman in golden dress is Empress Anna herself.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AValery_Jacobi_Ice_House.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/CWA%3B_%22The_New_Deal_Ice_Palace%22%3B_Lake_Bemidji%2C_Minnesota_-_DPLA_-_0746a82807f00fbe039585a2701afeaf.gif/500px-CWA%3B_%22The_New_Deal_Ice_Palace%22%3B_Lake_Bemidji%2C_Minnesota_-_DPLA_-_0746a82807f00fbe039585a2701afeaf.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/CWA%3B_%22The_New_Deal_Ice_Palace%22%3B_Lake_Bemidji%2C_Minnesota_-_DPLA_-_0746a82807f00fbe039585a2701afeaf.gif/500px-CWA%3B_%22The_New_Deal_Ice_Palace%22%3B_Lake_Bemidji%2C_Minnesota_-_DPLA_-_0746a82807f00fbe039585a2701afeaf.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Civil Works Administration: \"The Indian New Deal Ice Palace\", Lake Bemidji, Minnesota--1934","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACWA%3B_%22The_New_Deal_Ice_Palace%22%3B_Lake_Bemidji%2C_Minnesota_-_DPLA_-_0746a82807f00fbe039585a2701afeaf.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/BurstBark.jpg/120px-BurstBark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/BurstBark.jpg/250px-BurstBark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/BurstBark.jpg/120px-BurstBark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABurstBark.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Frost-Flower-4.JPG/250px-Frost-Flower-4.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https: